  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between cholic acid and Cytochrome c oxidase subunit 7B, mitochondrial, through a chain of targets involving N-Formylmethionine. Cholic acid is identified as a target of multiple cytochrome c oxidase subunit proteins, including subunit 2, 7C, and 5A, all of which are targeted by N-Formylmethionine. This indicates that cholic acid may interact with these subunits through a common intermediary, N-Formylmethionine, which appears to be a key mediator in the pathway. The high scores across the three paths (final_score=0.7391) suggest a strong and consistent relationship, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a possible role for cholic acid in modulating the activity of these subunits, potentially through the regulation of N-Formylmethionine, which in turn influences the function of the cytochrome c oxidase complex. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the biological network and the importance of further investigation into the molecular interactions involved.",
